### Rebase onto master (GH #60) — a third authority hole, 2026-08-24
Rebased onto 5822455 (clean, no conflicts). GH #60's `honor_gitignore`
(DEFAULT ON) drops `.as` files at DISCOVERY time, before `source_file_included`
runs, so `dependency_closure_complete` could be true while the pool was missing
own-module files. The game compiles gitignored files — gitignore is a git
concept, not a compile concept — so a namespace member declared only in a
generated-but-gitignored source was reported as `No matching symbol`.
Reproduced, then fenced.

The condition is "at least one `.as` file was actually dropped", NOT "honoring
is enabled": honoring is the default, so gating on the flag would disarm the
rule in nearly every repo — a vacuously silent rule is worse than the bug.
`project::discover` now returns a `Discovery { files, gitignore_excluded }`
unconditionally; `load_plugin_workspace` folds the count into
`dependency_closure_complete`. `log_excluded_count` keeps its DEBUG gate but no
longer re-derives the number (it no longer runs a walk of its own).

The baseline for the count comes from the SAME `ignore::WalkBuilder` with only
`git_ignore`/`git_exclude` flipped off, not from `discover_recursive` — one
traversal engine for both passes, so the count cannot drift from the kept set
and the crate's symlink-loop handling applies to both.

Cost, measured on tests/fixtures/tm-editor-plus-plus (263 `.as` files, release):
honoring walk 1.28 ms, baseline walk 0.65 ms, `discover()` total 2.24 ms,
against a ~4.7 s full check — the extra pass is ~0.01% of a check.

Dependency side checked: NOT affected. A resolved dep contributes only its
explicit `[script] exports`/`shared_exports` paths via
`deps::collect_export_files` -> `resolve_plugin_file`, read directly; no
discovery walk and no `DiscoveryOptions`, so gitignore never filters dep files
(`.op` archives read from the ZIP, likewise). No dep-side treatment needed.

### Review pass 2 (post-rebase, PASS) + the five-condition list, 2026-08-24
`ccc @cx-reviewer` pass 2 returned PASS on the rebased state. Two findings,
both fixed by it and both verified independently here:

* `fix(workspace): disarm namespace checks for missing exports` — resolving a
  dependency was not enough. A dep whose declared
  `[script] exports`/`shared_exports` include a MISSING or UNREADABLE file
  still counted as authoritative, so its partial namespace surface produced
  false `No matching symbol`. `ResolvedDependency` now reports
  `unloaded_exports` (directory and `.op` shapes alike) and the loader tracks
  `incomplete_export_surfaces`.
* `fix(typecheck): fence Tests engine namespace` — `Tests` is an Openplanet
  CORE namespace and was absent from
  `is_engine_namespace`, so a plugin-local `namespace Tests { … }` (a very
  likely name for test helpers) armed the rule against game-owned `Tests::`
  calls with no typedb loaded. Verified against the fixture typedb: `Tests`
  really is there, and it was the ONLY gap — diffing all typedb leading
  segments against the static list now yields nothing.

Added here: `engine_namespace_list_covers_every_typedb_namespace`, a
maintenance guard asserting every typedb namespace is in
`is_engine_namespace`. A typedb refresh that adds a namespace now fails in
CI rather than as a false `No matching symbol` in someone's plugin. Proven
red by removing `Tests` (both it and the reviewer's regression fail), green
when restored.

The authority conditions are now enumerated ONCE, as a numbered list with a
one-line "why" each, on
`workspace::load::PluginWorkspaceLoad::dependency_closure_complete`; the
predicate carries `// (n)` markers in the same order, and the mirrors in
`symbols::table`, `analysis_snapshot` and `checker` point at that list
instead of restating a subset (two of them had already drifted to a stale
three-condition version). Five conditions: real disk root; every declared
dependency resolved; every resolved dep contributed all declared exports; no
`source_paths`/`ignore_paths`; gitignore dropped no `.as` file.

Coordinator decision recorded: the `DEPENDENCY_<ID>`-define fix is B019, NOT
this branch. The four/five-condition guard stays as-is here.
